From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hipfire-windows <hipfire-windows@example.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:01:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] rdna-compute: skip /proc/meminfo on Windows UMA path

On UMA APUs (e.g. Strix Halo gfx1151), device_mem_info queries
/proc/meminfo (MemAvailable) to estimate host RAM available for GTT
allocations. This is a Linux-only path that returns None on Windows,
causing the UMA free-memory query to fail spuriously.

Add a #[cfg(windows)] early return that trusts hipMemGetInfo's free
value directly. On Windows, hipMemGetInfo already reports the UMA
carve-out free bytes correctly, so the Linux host-available adjustment
is unnecessary and unavailable.

Signed-off-by: hipfire-windows <hipfire-windows@example.com>
---
 crates/rdna-compute/src/dispatch.rs | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/rdna-compute/src/dispatch.rs b/crates/rdna-compute/src/dispatch.rs
index b568930..a7ee254 100644
--- a/crates/rdna-compute/src/dispatch.rs
+++ b/crates/rdna-compute/src/dispatch.rs
@@ -1559,6 +1559,15 @@ impl Gpu {
         if !self.is_uma() {
             return Ok((free, total));
         }
+        // Windows: `hipMemGetInfo` already reports the UMA carve-out free bytes
+        // correctly. The Linux host-available adjustment
+        // (`uma_memory::device_free_from` via `/proc/meminfo` MemAvailable)
+        // is unavailable on Windows and would spuriously return None, so skip
+        // it and trust the HIP-reported free value directly.
+        #[cfg(windows)]
+        {
+            return Ok((free, total));
+        }
         use crate::uma_memory;
         let carveout_total = self
             .hip
